-- The Eliot test framework as a package.
--
-- **The root package is the framework and the runner both.** `root` is `src/`, at `.` because its
-- directory is the repository's own, and the `main` in it is `eliot.test.Runner` — a fact about this
-- package, stated by this package, which is how a consumer's suite gets an entry point without naming
-- anybody's internals. A project that deps this one and declares no `main` of its own has exactly one
-- in its closure, which is what makes `eliot build test` work anywhere.
--
-- Both layers of the base are named, because `src` resolves against what it declares and nothing
-- else: the assertions and the mocks are written over `eliot.collection.List`, `eliot.file` and
-- `eliot.system`, and the runner reaches every suite in a program through `eliot.compiler.Reflect`,
-- which the `lang` layer declares rather than `stdlib`.
--
-- **No platform in the root package**, deliberately and load-bearingly: a framework is as
-- platform-independent as what it tests, and a consumer inheriting `//jvm` from here could never
-- build for anything else. `runner` and `test` name it, and nothing depends on either of them.
--
-- `runner` is the executable this repository ships and declares no `main` of its own — it inherits the
-- root package's through `dep //root`, because there is one runner and it is the one consumers get.
-- `test` is this repository's own suite, at `test/src`, and it runs by the same entry point for the
-- same reason.
--
-- `v0.1` is the floor because that is where the layers' `plugin` clauses start: a tag that declares no
-- plugin ships no compiler a consumer can find, so `eliot build` against `v0.0` correctly refuses.
-- Nothing here needs anything newer than `v0.1`'s sources.

package root {
  at .
  dep github.com/robertbraeutigam/eliot//lang v0.1
  dep github.com/robertbraeutigam/eliot//stdlib v0.1
  main eliot.test.Runner
}

package runner {
  dep //root
  dep github.com/robertbraeutigam/eliot//jvm v0.1
}

package test {
  dep //root
  dep github.com/robertbraeutigam/eliot//jvm v0.1
}
